#edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $5 \\div \\dfrac{1}{15}$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073470 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a09cb492-4d6a-54ee-884e-fc3ce58bf997" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073470 #edb/ref 1074 "To divide a whole number by a unit fraction, we multiply the whole number by the fraction's denominator:\n\n$$\n5 \\div \\dfrac{1}{15} = 5 \\times 15 = 75\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073471 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13725" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073471 #edb/ref 1071 "Johnny has $5$ kilograms of wheat flour with which he wants to make some pizzas. If each pizza needs $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ of a kilogram of wheat flour, how many pizzas can Johnny make?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073471 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bdc09ee6-a719-5dad-b85e-acb7cdc92458" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073471 #edb/ref 1074 "To determine the number of pizzas that Johnny can make, we divide the amount of wheat flour by the amount of wheat flour each pizza needs.\n\n$$\n5 \\div \\dfrac{1}{10}\n$$\n\nTo divide a whole number by a unit fraction, we multiply the whole number by the fraction's denominator:\n\n$$\n5 \\div \\dfrac{1}{10} = 5 \\times 10 = 50\n$$\n\nTherefore, Johnny can make $50$ pizzas." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073901 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073901 #edb/ref 1039 "Dividing a Whole Number by a Unit Fraction When the Denominator has One Digit" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073901 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073901 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "86c1c87e-1069-52cb-9b60-0c1d9439685c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073902 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073902 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073902 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 1759218607